            <ArticleTitle>High-attenuation crescent sign on computed tomography in acute abdominal aortic aneurysm.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>988.e1</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1016/j.ajem.2014.12.038</ELocationID>
            <ELocationID EIdType="pii" ValidYN="Y">S0735-6757(14)00940-1</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>We present an interesting radiologic finding in a 65-year-old gentleman who attended our emergency department (ED)with sudden-onset severe abdominal pain. Non–contrast-enhanced computed tomography of the abdomen revealed a 7-cm abdominal aortic aneurysm (AAA)which demonstrated the high-attenuation crescent sign (HACS).</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
